{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced","id":983758,"title":"Can Awakened Be Embraced?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T22:22:08-07:00","id":983758,"title":"Can Awakened Be Embraced?","content":"I know the rules as written is no what i'm asking more is if a kindred tries to embrace one of the Awakened what happens? What is it about a mage that stops the embrace? I know why for all the other lines but Mages are always portrayed as just Humans who know the right secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2107-wiwuno","name":"Wiwuno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:27:14-07:00","id":983759,"title":"","content":"They die. Simply put, their souls (well, their Gnosis to be more specific) are completely incompatible with the Embrace. It can't be replaced/turned into/coexist beside/whatever a Vampires Beast.<br /> <br /> While mages might seem perfectly human, the nature of their soul has changed considerably due to their Awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-08-2016, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:33:51-07:00","id":983761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=983759#post983759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They die. Simply put, their souls (well, their Gnosis to be more specific) are completely incompatible with the Embrace. It can't be replaced/turned into/coexist beside/whatever a Vampires Beast.<br /> <br /> While mages might seem perfectly human, the nature of their soul has changed considerably due to their Awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, this. We're the most human<i>-looking </i>of all monsters. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:38:01-07:00","id":983764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wiwuno</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced#post983758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the rules as written is no what i'm asking more is if a kindred tries to embrace one of the Awakened what happens? What is it about a mage that stops the embrace? I know why for all the other lines but Mages are always portrayed as just Humans who know the right secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are not just humans who know the right secrets. If that were the case, anyone could become a Mage simply by being taught. A Mage'a soul is fundamentally altered by Awakening - it no longer contains a shard of Abyss, it is no longer harmed by magic and it no longer causes Paradox or Dissonance. And most significantly, it is connected to the Supernal via a Watchtower, which is what allows the Mage to actually do magic. Why do these changes to the soul make a Mage unable to be Embraced? That's a Mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:50:53-07:00","id":983767,"title":"","content":"There is a certain class of spirits that can bring a dead person back to life, provided they haven't been dead too long and you still have the body. I believe it also specifically mentioned that werewolves stop being werewolves, and mages stop being mages, though.<br /> <br /> I imagine if you went this route, a werewolf could theoretically be brought back as a wolf-blooded and then eventually awaken. They'd almost certainly awaken to the Primal Wilds, though? As for vampires - I guess it depends on how quickly they decay, I've forgotten how it works in 2E Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:51:37-07:00","id":983768,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, the Tremere Legacy claim that this was done to them. But Left-Hand Path expanded on their background a lot and may have changed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:57:03-07:00","id":983771,"title":"","content":"The Awakened soul has developed a direct channel into the energies of the Supernal World. Even a narrow channel of this power has to be moderated by the shape of Wisdom to keep the mage from burning out in some way or another. It's not too hard to imagine that might somehow interfere with the Embrace of the Blood under normal circumstances.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you dig back into the history of the Tremere liches, you may recall that few conclusions are absolute in the Chronicles of Darkness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:59:27-07:00","id":983792,"title":"","content":"Vampires can't embrace mages, just like any other supernatural being. <br /> <br /> Strix, on enother hand, <i>can</i> use Synthesis if they're possessing a mage; it's the CofD's route to making strange hybrid vampire-monsters. And the creature who turned the Tremere into vampires may not have been a member of one of the five Clans...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:15:03-07:00","id":983803,"title":"","content":"The timid are true vampires? (I've read left hand legacies, but my mind is a sieve and I don't remember the Timori being directly vampires now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:20:15-07:00","id":983805,"title":"","content":"No, but they used to be at ine point in their history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:21:33-07:00","id":983807,"title":"","content":"And you mean Tremere. Timori (&quot;the fearful&quot;; it means &quot;we're scared if them&quot; not &quot;they're scared of everything&quot;) are an entirely seperate oup of Reaper-Liches, and one of the iconic Banisher Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T01:47:18-07:00","id":983826,"title":"","content":"Yep, just rereading the above I slapped my head for mixing them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:10:18-07:00","id":983904,"title":"","content":"Wait, so are Timoris in 2nd Ed actually full-on reapers? In first ed it was possible for one to survive their predations with everything but their magical bits intact. (though they were kind of logistical nightmares run).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:16:40-07:00","id":983908,"title":"","content":"Timori were in the Banisher book, they harvest Gnosis, which is basically the magical part of the soul of a Mage.<br /> <br /> Tremere harvest the structural integrity part of the soul that keeps identity and motivation from collapsing in on itself and they can take that from anyone.<br /> <br /> Both legacies are a kind of Reaper, but the Tremere are the more traditional kind. Neither has gotten the full 2e treatment yet.<br /> <br /> Either process can be survived, though eventually if the Timori harvest enough Gnosis from a Mage I believe it does kill them. I can't remember exactly though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:25:27-07:00","id":983910,"title":"","content":"The effects of the Timori don't really map to the soul-loss conditions at all, and mortals aren't even part of the equation.<br /> <br /> If you lose all your gnosis you become a sleeper with only vague notions of their former life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:08:17-07:00","id":983939,"title":"","content":"That's because, like I mentioned, different part of the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T10:02:24-07:00","id":983957,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a whole vampire Lineage that was made up of nothing but former mages? But the transformation into a vampire stripped them of the ability to use all but I think 2 arcanum? Now if I remember right that was oWoD but it might start us off as a sort of starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T11:41:02-07:00","id":983992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=983957#post983957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a whole vampire Lineage that was made up of nothing but former mages? But the transformation into a vampire stripped them of the ability to use all but I think 2 arcanum? Now if I remember right that was oWoD but it might start us off as a sort of starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might be thinking of Awakening's Tremere, discussed above.<br /> <br /> The oWoD's Tremere vampires began with ex-mages, but they found they'd lost all access to Awakened magick upon becoming vampires. Soon enough, they started Embracing non-mages, needing new recruits in pretty short order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T05:16:09-07:00","id":984355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=983992#post983992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might be thinking of Awakening's Tremere, discussed above.<br /> <br /> The oWoD's Tremere vampires began with ex-mages, but they found they'd lost all access to Awakened magick upon becoming vampires. Soon enough, they started Embracing non-mages, needing new recruits in pretty short order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, but couldn't we carry over the idea of the Tremere Vampire from Masquerade and give them a bloodline (I'm thinking Deava) specific devotion that say grants them the death Arcanium? Though they don't gain the Atainments and may only have their free reach (grasp) and cannot risk paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T06:07:22-07:00","id":984360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=984355#post984355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh, but couldn't we carry over the idea of the Tremere Vampire from Masquerade and give them a bloodline (I'm thinking Deava) specific devotion that say grants them the death Arcanium? Though they don't gain the Atainments and may only have their free reach (grasp) and cannot risk paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds like a way too complicated way of doing it, and either stupidly OP or weak depending on how you go about it. Especially since we have a perfectly good set of rules for mage-like magic already in Blood Sorcery the book. If I were to do the Tremere as a bloodline I'd make them a universal bloodline who gets a unique blood sorcery as their fourth discipline with a hermetic motif to them (lots of magic circles, rods, wands and staves). The Blood Sorcery works better as well too, given how cwod tremere were mage inspired but not actually given access to spheres, which is what Blood Sorcery basically is, mage inspired without actual arcana access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:18:56-07:00","id":984991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=984360#post984360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That sounds like a way too complicated way of doing it, and either stupidly OP or weak depending on how you go about it. Especially since we have a perfectly good set of rules for mage-like magic already in Blood Sorcery the book. If I were to do the Tremere as a bloodline I'd make them a universal bloodline who gets a unique blood sorcery as their fourth discipline with a hermetic motif to them (lots of magic circles, rods, wands and staves). The Blood Sorcery works better as well too, given how cwod tremere were mage inspired but not actually given access to spheres, which is what Blood Sorcery basically is, mage inspired without actual arcana access.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works. I wasn't familiar with that book, I mainly use Vampires as antagonist and background rather than PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:23:07-07:00","id":984996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=983764#post983764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are not just humans who know the right secrets. If that were the case, anyone could become a Mage simply by being taught. A Mage'a soul is fundamentally altered by Awakening - it no longer contains a shard of Abyss, it is no longer harmed by magic and it no longer causes Paradox or Dissonance. And most significantly, it is connected to the Supernal via a Watchtower, which is what allows the Mage to actually do magic. Why do these changes to the soul make a Mage unable to be Embraced? That's a Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The mystery of why they die could be a great character motivation, but I wouldn't change the fact they die. Usually in my games that supernatural blood of all types is somewhat addicting, and it provides some cool bonus. Like drugs can in CoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Running: <a href=\"https://shield-bearers.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Shield Bearers - W:TF 2nd</a><br /> Currently Planning: The Dead End Kids - CoD<br /> Untilted Tenra Bansho Zero game<br /> Currently Playing: <a href=\"http://theunusualsuspects.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Unusual Suspects - D:td</a>, I am playing <a href=\"http://www.noordinaryobsession.com/2016/08/19/unusual-suspects-naturalist/\" target=\"_blank\">The Naturalist</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2293-salientmind","name":"salientmind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T12:45:32-07:00","id":985006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=984355#post984355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahh, but couldn't we carry over the idea of the Tremere Vampire from Masquerade and give them a bloodline (I'm thinking Deava) specific devotion that say grants them the death Arcanium? Though they don't gain the Atainments and may only have their free reach (grasp) and cannot risk paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creating Vampires that use Mage Arcanum, powers that work completely differently from Disciplines, is just going to be messy. What I would suggest is taking a series of Rotes (forgive me I'm working from a mostly 1E Mage frame of reference), stripping them down into something that doesn't rely on Mage-specific mechanics, then stringing them together into a Discipline and calking over the cracks with Vampire mechanics. Yeah you'll be sacrificing a lot of flexibility, but that seems like something that would get lost transforming from a Mage into a Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T00:16:56-07:00","id":985303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=985006#post985006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating Vampires that use Mage Arcanum, powers that work completely differently from Disciplines, is just going to be messy. What I would suggest is taking a series of Rotes (forgive me I'm working from a mostly 1E Mage frame of reference), stripping them down into something that doesn't rely on Mage-specific mechanics, then stringing them together into a Discipline and calking over the cracks with Vampire mechanics. Yeah you'll be sacrificing a lot of flexibility, but that seems like something that would get lost transforming from a Mage into a Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For 2e if you want playable vampires just by using MtAw rules, I'd just make them a proximi dynasty. Tie their curses to drinking blood, fire and sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:54:20-07:00","id":985321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=984360#post984360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That sounds like a way too complicated way of doing it, and either stupidly OP or weak depending on how you go about it. Especially since we have a perfectly good set of rules for mage-like magic already in Blood Sorcery the book. If I were to do the Tremere as a bloodline I'd make them a universal bloodline who gets a unique blood sorcery as their fourth discipline with a hermetic motif to them (lots of magic circles, rods, wands and staves). The Blood Sorcery works better as well too, given how cwod tremere were mage inspired but not actually given access to spheres, which is what Blood Sorcery basically is, mage inspired without actual arcana access.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why not just a hermetic based Covenant dedicated to &quot;Learning magic&quot; and &quot;using it to gain control of vampire society&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T02:40:53-07:00","id":985327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983758-can-awakened-be-embraced?p=985321#post985321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Why not just a hermetic based Covenant dedicated to &quot;Learning magic&quot; and &quot;using it to gain control of vampire society&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A covenant works as well, in fact I think it works better, but if you want to keep the lineage focus of the original tremere then a bloodline is a better way of going about it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:48:25-07:00","id":985782,"title":"","content":"Well, I know that Chris Falco came up with a CoD Tremere write up that I think is the best I've seen yet. Definitely on my list of things to get a ST to allow. I would love to see what he'd write up for Tremere Ghouls, like there are for other clans/covenants . I'd like to see what others would come up with for various supernatural splats that have undergone Strix Synthesis, especially Mages. And I've tried to come up with &quot;Vampire&quot; legacies for various Paths/Orders, especially a Tamer of blood that was more vampire blood bond/Ghouling than creating sympathy for spell casting. I know that there were a number of legacies in 1st Ed that could emulate/transition into different beings. I'd imagine that would be a route to take to come up with a Vampire Mage, though I know that various paths and orders would have different views on how to go about it.(almost certainly left-handed) No thoughts on how they'd handle banes though. &quot;<i>No Edward, having your legacy sparkle does not count as a bane!&quot;<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br /> <br /> I have no idea whether there are any custom legacies that people have come up with or posted that fit this theme, but I'm always on the lookout. There have been quite a number of custom legacies that I thought I'd definitely like to have a character join. Favorites so far are 2nd Ed Tamers of the Wind, and proindrakenzol's Thaumatech Engineer. I'd have to search for the poster of 2nd Ed Tamers of the Wind, but that isn't an insult, and I love how it's written, both as is and the optional Mind Attainment path that follows the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12527-thearcane","name":"TheArcane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12527_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}